  "01a12a11-9c9d-75b0-bd52-223d5329bfdb",
  {
    "submission": "update.json",
    "summary": "Investigated the receiver side of the leadership-transfer order (TimeoutNow) as an authority transition, and recorded one unresolved configuration-state question.\n\nSourced defect candidate (A2, authority transition): `Raft.timeoutNow` (raft.go:2209-2214) is the one authority-bearing RPC handler that binds to nothing. It clears the known leader, sets state Candidate and sets candidateFromLeadershipTransfer=true, ignoring the RPC header identity and the configuration, while `TimeoutNowRequest` (commands.go:206-208) carries only RPCHeader and therefore no term at all. The producer only sends it after catching the target up (raft.go:1003-1032), a precondition the receiver cannot verify, and the order simultaneously disables both disruption guards: runCandidate skips pre-vote (raft.go:285-308) and voters skip the known-leader rejection (raft.go:1603-1656). Contrast: appendEntries and installSnapshot both reject/ignore a sender term below the receiver's current term (raft.go:1453-1463, 1833-1841).\n\nLocal native feedback (not formal evidence): the requested harness (draft/assurance_timeoutnow.go) in a normally bootstrapped, fault-free 3-node in-memory cluster shows the steady state (leader at term 2, target Follower at term 2), a control stale-term RequestVote from a claimed sender 'ghost-not-in-config' leaving the target unmoved, and then one TimeoutNow from the same non-member claimed sender driving the target from Follower(term 2) to Leader(term 3) and deposing the serving leader (Follower, term 3) within 2s. This is an authority/disruption defect; no state-machine safety violation is claimed, and the spoofed-identity route overlaps with transport-level trust, so the experiment asks for the controller's fixed-input execution and comparison. `validate --submission update.json` returns valid:true.\n\nSecond, unresolved question (no mechanism claim, no knowledge entry): running the captured TestRaft_ProtocolVersion_Upgrade_2_3 locally failed 2 of 3 isolated runs with 'peer mismatch', where an old follower reported the 2-server bootstrap configuration for the whole 5s EnsureSamePeers window while the added server reported 3 servers; GetConfiguration returns an atomically published latestConfiguration (api.go:897-903), and a candidate production path is the appendEntries truncation rollback (raft.go:1526-1532) plus duplicate-skip. Instrumented re-implementations of the same scenario converged within 250ms on every run, so the mechanism is recorded as a registered gap rather than a finding."
  }
